  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d8e9c4ee2d087d04d9b8cdf89c4f21bd, type: 3}
  m_Name: Lore1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  id: Lore_1
  title: Day one
  fullText: 'If thou hast awakened here once more, then were our efforts in vain.


    The
    cards were ill-played,

    or perchance chosen for us long ere we did arrive
    in this cursed place.


    I remember the bitter wind.

    Fading lights.

    The
    moon above.


    And her.


    The lady speaketh not the whole truth.

    Mark
    well the manner in which she speaketh of the cards.

    Mark also her hands
    about the crystal sphere.


    She knoweth already how this tale doth end.


    Tread
    with caution.


    And strive to remember.'
